  "about": "DATA for read-data/plain-privacy-pass.mjs: what words meant for strangers may never carry, found without a model. `identifying` are the patterns (an address, a handle, a long number, an amount of money, a key), each with why; `removed_mark` is the one neutral mark a redaction leaves, itself a finding; `not_identifying` are capitalised words that name no one; `entity_words` and `places` are generic dictionaries every shared text is checked against. A person's own words (their names, their never-publish list) are their records, passed in by the caller, never here.",
